      "hints": [
        "Set $8x^4 + 24x^2 + 21 = 34x^2 + 19$.",
        "Rearrange into a quadratic in $x^2$.",
        "Solve for $x^2$ and state the valid non-negative values of $x$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Equate $ff(x)$ to $34x^2 + 19$:\n$$8x^4 + 24x^2 + 21 = 34x^2 + 19$$",
        "Collect all terms on one side:\n$$8x^4 - 10x^2 + 2 = 0 \\implies 4(x^2)^2 - 5(x^2) + 1 = 0$$",
        "Factorise the quadratic in $x^2$:\n$$(4x^2 - 1)(x^2 - 1) = 0 \\implies x^2 = \\frac{1}{4} \\quad\\text{or}\\quad x^2 = 1$$",
        "Take square roots, enforcing the domain condition $x \\ge 0$:\n$$x = \\frac{1}{2} \\quad\\text{or}\\quad x = 1$$"
